Wang tiles ⭐⭐⭐

These are incredibly relevant.

Wang tiles are tiles whose edges have "colors." Tiles are only placed next to matching edge colors.

Your chunk system is basically Wang tiles at the chunk scale.

Wave Function Collapse (WFC) ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

This is the biggest one I'd recommend reading about.

Despite the intimidating name, it's essentially:

"Choose tiles while respecting neighbor constraints."

You don't have to implement the full algorithm. Even understanding its concepts—neighbor compatibility and constraint propagation—can greatly improve your chunk system.

Many indie games use simplified WFC.

